<title>UK: Major rejects EMU central tax, spending controls.</title>
<headline>Major rejects EMU central tax, spending controls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Wednesday he would not take Britain into a single European currency if it meant surrendering control of spending and tax to a central body.</p>
<p>&quot;Each and every member of my cabinet would utterly reject the concept of spending control and tax control being exercised centrally if we entered a single currency and that were to be the outcome over a period of years,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
